WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:06.190
You are attempting to access Terminal 7 at
Site-119.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:12.830
By continuing, you are confirming that you:
have permission to access this file, have

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:19.220
submitted your Last Will and Testament to
the SCP Foundation HR Department, have said

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:25.840
goodbye to all of your family and loved ones,
and consent to the probability of a swift,

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.109
painful death.

00:00:27.109 --> 00:00:33.030
You are not currently under any threat, but
continuing to access this file will change

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.030
that.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:43.670
Please look into the screen to confirm your
identity via retinal scan.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:48.290
Do not blink.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:53.579
WARNING: the threat is approaching rapidly.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:57.950
You have a limited amount of time to review
the contents of this file.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:02.180
Remember that this terminal has been permanently
contained.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:08.100
Mobile Task Force members are aware of your
location, and on standby, but they will likely

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.329
not be able to save you.

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:13.729
It is only a matter of time now.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:18.569
SCP-2744 is a bipedal humanoid creature with
a height of two meters.

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:23.960
Its face is covered with a torn white burlap
cloth, with a large aluminum zipper across

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.029
its mouth.

00:01:25.029 --> 00:01:30.849
Though its true name is unknown, it is to
be referred to by codename “Tattletale.”

00:01:30.849 --> 00:01:33.720
The creature is extremely dangerous, and hostile.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.399
It has been determined to target anyone who
attempts to investigate it or learn the nature

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:39.499
of its identity.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:43.639
It cannot be restrained or prevented from
reaching its target.

00:01:43.639 --> 00:01:45.639
Once it has set its sights on you, you cannot
hide.

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:47.029
You cannot run.

00:01:47.029 --> 00:01:50.429
There is no escape.

00:01:50.429 --> 00:01:55.340
The entity is currently uncontained, but steps
have been taken to limit its potential for

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.429
damage.

00:01:56.429 --> 00:02:00.789
Only this terminal has complete read and edit
access to the file.

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:05.649
Once someone has linked with the terminal,
all members of MTF-Epsilon 99 are stationed

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:07.959
at the entrance to the containment cell.

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:11.780
The entity may not be discussed outside of
the containment cell.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:17.670
If you speak about the Tattletale entity outside
of this room, you will be immediately terminated.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.040
Once you have accessed this file, you are
considered lost.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.280
Tattletale was first encountered in the Eurtec
nexus.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:28.709
The nexus is an underground free port where
a number of anomalous entities live without

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:29.900
fear of exposure.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:36.170
It’s also a network of underground tunnels
used for smuggling and other unsavory business.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.769
Following a series of unsolved murders and
disappearances, the Global Occult Coalition

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:43.099
reached out to the Foundation for help.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:49.359
A research team was deployed to investigate,
consisting of Agent Jaime Greene, Adam Smith,

00:02:49.359 --> 00:02:54.170
Sammi Radcliffe, Dr. Stephen House, and Agent
William Miller.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.489
Agent Miller was outfitted with a body cam,
which captured the following events.

00:02:58.489 --> 00:03:02.560
Miller met with the rest of the team in an
underground house in the Eurtec Nexus.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.760
Inside, he found a blood-stained room thrown
into chaos, items turned over and scattered

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:08.849
across the room.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:12.680
There was an unidentified body found inside
the house.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:17.959
The deceased suffered from deep wounds across
their chest that tore off skin and muscle,

00:03:17.959 --> 00:03:20.879
revealing the organs and broken bones beneath.

00:03:20.879 --> 00:03:25.480
Their face was riddled with large bite marks,
and their nose was missing entirely.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:29.849
Though there were bits of flesh and blood
all throughout the room, the nose was not

00:03:29.849 --> 00:03:30.849
found.

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:36.540
While searching the room, Miller found a blood-spattered
note with the words “HELP…WORKERS” written,

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.340
along with a phone number.

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.639
As the group continued to investigate, they
suddenly heard something moving and scratching

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:43.760
in the walls.

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:45.620
Tension began to rise.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.770
Was the killer still in their midst?

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:52.639
Did they need to act now, before it had the
chance to give them the same gruesome fate?

00:03:52.639 --> 00:03:55.440
Radcliffe shot at the wall, and a rat crawled
out.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.629
They were safe.

00:03:56.629 --> 00:03:57.629
For now.

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:02.209
The body couldn’t be identified and was
classified as ENTITY VICTIM 12.

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:06.319
The note recovered from the crime scene led
the Foundation to an attempted human - and

00:04:06.319 --> 00:04:08.819
nonhuman entity - trafficking scheme.

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:13.849
Eight missing persons and creatures were recovered
from a warehouse and interviewed.

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:18.410
This new chapter of the investigation left
the team with more questions than answers,

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:23.770
and after an anonymous tip, the task force
reached out to an unnamed lizard man, believed

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:28.980
to be a member of the mysterious Fae, who
was reported to have helpful information.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.940
The lizard informed Agents Miller and Radcliffe
that he had seen something troubling.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:40.520
He couldn’t remember the specific details,
but a monster had come to SCP-4000, an enchanted

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:45.860
forest and the home of the Fae, and spoken
to someone the lizard man had once known.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:51.160
He followed them home but found only a mangled
corpse and a room drenched in blood.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:56.800
One detail stood out in particular: the lizard
man said his dead friend had been robbed of

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:59.849
a name, left “a nameless husk.”

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:04.340
Whatever had killed them, it had erased their
very identity.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.210
Even the interviewee, who had once considered
the victim a friend, could no longer remember

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.540
who they were.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:15.720
This would be nightmarish for anyone, but
especially a member of the Fae, as names hold

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.280
a great deal of importance for them.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:22.169
When Agents Radcliffe and Miller returned
from conducting their interviews, they were

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:25.960
informed that four new anomalous murders had
occurred in their absence.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:32.129
Each body had the same wounds, deep lacerations
on the torso, and large chunks of the face

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:33.500
bitten off.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:38.870
This was troubling enough, but even more concerning
was a series of unauthorized changes to the

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:44.930
Foundation’s employee database, which occurred
at the same time as the killings.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:50.590
Four employee personnel files had been inexplicably
deleted, to match the four unidentified bodies

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:51.889
that were found.

00:05:51.889 --> 00:05:56.879
There was reason to believe that these four
new victims had all been Foundation personnel,

00:05:56.879 --> 00:06:01.970
but no one could remember their names, and
no one recognized their faces.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.400
The remaining records confirmed that there
had been seven members of the task force dispatched

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.930
to handle these unsolved murders.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.819
Four were gone, lost from the world and from
collective memory.

00:06:12.819 --> 00:06:18.849
Now, only three remained: Sammi Radcliffe,
Stephen House, and William Miller.

00:06:18.849 --> 00:06:23.600
Miller and Radcliffe met to discuss this new
development and realized that they were being

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:24.650
hunted.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:29.000
Something knew they were investigating it,
and it was taking out the research team one

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.099
by one.

00:06:30.099 --> 00:06:31.360
Four down.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:32.580
Three to go.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:37.259
The remaining researchers were ordered to
return to Site 119 for round-the-clock protection

00:06:37.259 --> 00:06:38.960
and surveillance.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.419
Stephen House ignored these orders and locked
himself away in a safehouse located within

00:06:43.419 --> 00:06:44.470
the Nexus.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:49.830
Radcliffe insisted that she and Miller follow
their orders and leave House behind, but Miller

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:50.909
refused.

00:06:50.909 --> 00:06:56.900
He would not leave a man behind, not after
losing the rest of the team, even if he couldn’t

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:58.120
remember them.

00:06:58.120 --> 00:07:01.850
Miller made his way to the safehouse and arrived
to find the door already open.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:05.540
He entered the building, searching for his
missing colleague.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:09.270
He called out, “Stephen?” and “Are you
here?”

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.680
but there was no response.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:16.080
His path wound between rows of shelves, down
pitch-black narrow hallways that seemed to

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.660
go on forever.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:21.860
Just when he thought Stephen might already
be lost, he heard a loud crash coming from

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:22.860
up ahead.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.860
He followed the sound down the hall, drawing
his gun just in case.

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:29.520
He turned to the left and saw another open
door.

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:32.360
Inside, there was a small janitor’s closet.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:36.770
A bucket was knocked over, and water had spilled
all over the floor.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:40.599
As Miller scanned the room, his eyes fell
on a limp body.

00:07:40.599 --> 00:07:42.350
It was Stephen House.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:46.759
Miller ran to his fallen colleague’s side,
crouching down to check his wounds.

00:07:46.759 --> 00:07:51.050
House’s body was horribly damaged, with
claw marks from his shoulder to his hip.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:55.900
There were puncture wounds across his hands
and arms, and his leg was broken, twisted

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:59.310
around until bone showed through the torn
skin.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:03.610
Afraid of what he would find, Miller reached
down to check the man’s pulse, but a hand

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:04.710
stopped him.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.979
Stephen House was still alive.

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:12.139
He struggled to speak, saying “I’m not
useless…I swear I’m not.”

00:08:12.139 --> 00:08:15.539
And then, one chilling word: “Run.”

00:08:15.539 --> 00:08:18.669
Behind Miller, something let out an inhuman
screech.

00:08:18.669 --> 00:08:23.340
He spun around to see what made the sound
and saw a creature lurching toward him.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:26.870
It was tall, humanoid in shape, but distinctly
monstrous.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:32.580
A zipper across its face was unzipped to reveal
teeth stained black and red with blood.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.520
The creature jumped on top of him, knocking
him to the ground.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:40.190
He thrashed and fought back, trying to throw
the monster off of him, but it sank its teeth

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:43.690
into his exposed forearm with a sickening
crunch.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:47.960
Fighting through the pain, Miller fired his
gun with his other hand, hitting the creature

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:48.960
in the neck.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.750
It screamed and recoiled, allowing Miller
to climb back onto his feet and fire several

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:54.950
more shots.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:59.640
The creature scuttled up the wall toward the
ceiling, evading Miller’s gunfire and advancing

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.660
toward him.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:04.520
Miller took a step back, but slipped in the
blood on the floor and fell onto his injured

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.520
arm.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:10.290
Helpless, Miller watched as the entity dove
down at him, snarling and ready to devour

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:11.290
him.

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:14.150
Before it reached him, the crack of a gunshot
rang out.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:17.610
Miller looked up to see Agent Radcliffe holding
a shotgun.

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.390
She had come to save him.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:23.590
The two ran back into the hall, the entity
close behind them, and took cover behind a

00:09:23.590 --> 00:09:25.130
large shelving unit.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:29.850
As the entity approached, hunting for them,
they tried to determine what to do next.

00:09:29.850 --> 00:09:33.640
Miller was frozen in place, shaken from all
he had seen.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.620
Radcliffe told him to run for the door.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:39.530
She stepped out from behind their cover and
drew the attention of the entity.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:43.950
She fired several more shots at it, then turned
to see if Miller had made it to safety.

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:47.000
As Miller begged Radcliffe to run, her shotgun
jammed.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.560
She had no time to escape, no way to defend
herself.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.400
Her words, before the monster descended on
her, were: “You’re not supposed to let

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.690
me die like this.”

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.080
With nothing else he could do, Miller ran.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:04.120
He ran as fast as he could, cradling his damaged
arm, listening to Radcliffe’s screams turn

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.270
to wet gurgles, and then silence.

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:11.640
He made it out of the building, where a team
of Foundation personnel were waiting to usher

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:12.910
him to safety.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:17.440
He was taken back to Site-119 and placed under
24-hour surveillance.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:20.890
The entity he encountered was entered into
the system.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:21.900
File complete.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:24.000
We hope it was worth it, Agent Miller.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.940
There isn’t much time left.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:26.940
It’s coming.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:28.220
You know that.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:33.390
Any minute now, it will creep up behind you
and sink its teeth into your skin, devouring

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:36.540
your body and your name in one fatal blow.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:37.540
What is it?

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:41.390
Is it simply a monster with an insatiable
appetite for human lives?

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.300
Perhaps it was once a human, too.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:48.430
A murder victim left unseen and unsolved,
that transformed into a creature intent on

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:50.200
erasing others.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:55.020
Perhaps it was an idea made real by people’s
fear of it, and that is why it’s so afraid

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.410
of being known.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:02.420
If the puzzle is solved, if it is truly understood,
perhaps the creature will simply cease to

00:11:02.420 --> 00:11:03.420
exist.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:05.310
There is screaming outside the room.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:06.310
Gunfire.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.300
Pounding on the walls.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:09.600
Protection is wearing thin.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.920
So, think.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.060
What was it?

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.060
What is it?

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.370
You only have a few moments left.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:18.190
What will you leave behind once it takes you?

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:19.200
Maybe it was fear.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:23.900
All of the victims were running from something,
hiding from an invisible demon.

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:28.710
Pain, feelings of inadequacy, the sheer terror
of the unknown.

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:33.410
Everyone trying to run, to deny their nightmares,
and pretend that sleeping with the lights

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:35.020
on would be enough.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:36.460
But it never is.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.110
The darkness always comes.

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:39.110
Here it comes.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:40.110
Congratulations, Agent Miller.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:41.440
You have officially completed the Tattletale
Simulation.

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:42.540
Congratulations, Agent Miller.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:46.030
You have officially completed the Tattletale
Simulation.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:50.790
You were successful in acting under pressure,
showing dedication to the mission and the

00:11:50.790 --> 00:11:54.740
cause, and valuing the lives of your colleagues
over your own safety.

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:59.390
Your results show high intelligence, problem-solving,
and critical thinking skills.

00:11:59.390 --> 00:12:04.700
The test was administered by Agent Sammi Radcliffe,
Agent Jaime Green, and Dr. Stephen House.

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:08.470
Though your work was impressive, you have
some areas for improvement.

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:12.400
You did not follow protocol when engaging
with the Tattletale entity, and you failed

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.940
to prevent the simulated deaths of Radcliffe,
Green, and House.

00:12:15.940 --> 00:12:17.350
Better luck next time!

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:21.420
Still, you displayed admirable selflessness
and devotion to the Foundation’s mission

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:24.360
of knowledge, information, and containment
of anomalies.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:27.150
You have been approved for fieldwork going
forward.

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:32.160
Now is a good time to celebrate, many others
who were given this test were not so lucky.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:37.430
The past 50 subjects to complete this simulation
failed under pressure and died of heart failure

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:39.380
when their fear got the best of them.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.380
But not you.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:43.860
You have the makings of a truly great agent
here at the SCP Foundation.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.790
We’ll be in touch soon.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:51.900
Now go check out “Procedure 110 Montauk
REVEALED - Fear Alone - SCP-231 Tale” and

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:57.440
“SCP-1025 - Encyclopedia of Common Diseases”
for more SCPs that will mess with your head!

